# about

## This is not a web browser

A web page is bytes from an address that can change at any time, running
scripts with the browser's full authority, leaving a history you cannot
prove. A पत्र (patra) page is the opposite on every point:

* a page is a content-addressed object: its hash is its address, and it cannot change
* a link resolves to exact content or not at all: there is no 404 that used to be something else
* a page's script is a cell with exactly the capabilities you grant, listed before it runs
* your history is the ledger: provable, replayable, undoable
* there are no cookies or trackers, because a page holds no capability it was not given

## The format

```
# heading        ## sub-heading
plain paragraphs, * list items, > quotations
=> target label  (target: hash, tag:name, page:title)
@cell code store[get] console[print]
```

=> page:home back to the start
